# Pipeline

This repository contains a cross-platform, extensible pipeline for building, testing and deploying projects. It is intentionally small and easily integrated into existing repositories or CI providers.

## Contents
- scripts/        - portable scripts to run pipeline stages (build/test/package/deploy)
- pipeline/       - pipeline stage implementations and helpers
- config/         - default configuration and environment templates
- tests/          - test harness and test suites

## Goals
- Provide a minimal, repeatable pipeline that runs locally or in CI
- Keep stage logic platform-agnostic (works on POSIX and Windows)
- Make it easy to extend and hook into CI providers (GitHub Actions, Azure Pipelines, GitLab CI, etc.)

## Quick start
Prerequisites:
- Git
- A shell (bash, PowerShell) or a container runtime (Docker)

Clone and run locally:

files:
# secrets:
#   airflow_fernet_key:
#     file: ./secrets/airflow_fernet_key
#   airflow_webserver_secret:
#     file: ./secrets/airflow_webserver_secret
#   airflow_api_jwt_secret:
#     file: ./secrets/airflow_api_jwt_secret
#   postgres_password:
#     file: ./secrets/postgres_password
#   mongo_root_password:
#     file: ./secrets/mongo_root_password

Bash / WSL:

docker compose pull

docker compose up -d

docker exec -it apiserver airflow users create \
   --username admin \
   --firstname Admin --lastname User \
   --role Admin \
   --email admin@yourco.com \
   --password 'S3cureP@ss!'

# # inside the broker container
kafka-configs --bootstrap-server broker:29092 \
   --alter --add-config 'SCRAM-SHA-512=[password=SuperSecret!]' \
   --entity-type users --entity-name app1

## CREAR LAS KEYS 
# 1) Ejecuta keytool desde un contenedor (JDK 17)
docker run --rm -v "${PWD}:/work" -w /work eclipse-temurin:17-jdk-jammy `
  keytool -genkeypair -alias kafka-broker `
  -keystore server.keystore.jks -storepass changeme_keystore `
  -keypass changeme_key -keyalg RSA -keysize 4096 -validity 3650 `
  -dname "CN=kafka.ecoceutics.com, OU=Dev, O=Ecoceutics, L=Barcelona, ST=Barcelona, C=ES" `
  -ext "SAN=dns:kafka.ecoceutics.com"
#  2) Exporta el certificado público (PEM)
docker run --rm -v "${PWD}:/work" -w /work eclipse-temurin:17-jdk-jammy `
  keytool -exportcert -alias kafka-broker `
  -keystore server.keystore.jks -storepass changeme_keystore `
  -rfc -file server.crt
# 3) Crea el truststore e importa el cert
docker run --rm -v "${PWD}:/work" -w /work eclipse-temurin:17-jdk-jammy `
  keytool -importcert -alias kafka-broker `
  -file server.crt -keystore server.truststore.jks `
  -storepass changeme_truststore -noprompt
# 4) Crea los archivos de contraseñas (una sola línea cada uno)
Set-Content -NoNewline -Path keystore_creds      -Value 'changeme_keystore'
Set-Content -NoNewline -Path key_creds           -Value 'changeme_key'
Set-Content -NoNewline -Path truststore_creds    -Value 'changeme_truststore'

